  "description": "A long traverse from Lazeshchyna to Yasinia over Petros (2,020 m), 33 km with 1,340 m of ascent — a full day or an overnight. About 10 km near the start are on a minor road, then tracks and footpaths climb to the ridge; OpenStreetMap tags part of the path as alpine hiking (SAC T4). Mapped along the way: Petros, Petrosul (1,848 m), several huts and camp spots, and one seasonal spring labelled as drying up, so carry water.\n\nRoute data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). OSM relation/8613349.\nCover photo: Володимир Тертишник / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons.",
